From c6618ab8184e13e1afdf91f52ac12b00154c6e68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:36:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] toolkit: Implements minimizing (miniaturizing) windows.

wlmtk_window_request_minimize() was a stub, so the title bar's minimize
button, and clients' xdg_toplevel.set_minimized did nothing.

A minimized window is hidden, but remains on its workspace and in the
task list. If it was activated, the topmost visible window gets activated
instead. Raising the window restores it: When selected in the task list
(Alt+Tab), when activated through xdg-activation, and so on. Unmapping
the window clears the state.

Until there is an icon area for mini-windows, this permits to get windows
out of the way, as with Window Maker's "Miniaturize".

* Adds wlmtk_workspace_minimize_window() and wlmtk_window_is_minimized().
* Adds the `WindowMinimize` action, and "Miniaturize" to the window menu.
* Forwards xdg_toplevel's request_minimize.

Adds a unit test.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
